      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "The Sumerian (or Akkadian) ceremonial name of the ziggurat at Kalhu is not recorded in extant Assyrian texts. An Akkadian text of the ninth-century-BC Assyrian king Shalmaneser III (r. 858\u2013824 BC) inscribed on two bricks discovered at Kalhu refer to the temple-tower as the \u201cziggurat of the god Ninurta.\u201d",
